1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.gamleskien.no/getperson.php?personID=I30525&tree=GamleSkien
2 CONT
2 CONT He was named Ellef Christopher Paus as a pun on the Norwegian word for eleventh, as he was the eleventh child of his parents. He was known only by the name of Christopher Paus. He was a businessman and a partner in the Manchester 
2 CONC and Bradford cotton and woolen textile export firm Blydt, Paus and Pace. He moved to Lübeck in the early 1860s and to Manchester a few years later, eventually settling in Bradford.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christopher_Paus_%281843%E2%80%931919%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Census 1911 https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XWJL-WWW
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ellen Lord in Manchester in 1870.
