1 OCCU Væreier, Væreier i Finnmark og Ordfører i Vardø, Kjøpmann
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/ft/person/pf01037570002248
2 CONT
2 CONT http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/ft/person/pf01036972000138
2 CONT
2 CONT http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/ft/person/pf01053257027735
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hemming Lauritz Brodtkorb'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hemming was a strange man. He was the one that build the dynasty of Brodtkorb in the town of Vardø. Before the second world war he owned to-third of the town Vardø, and he also owned 6 "fiskevær". His income in the thirties was ap
2 CONC pr. 34 million kroner.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1946 he moved to the town Lillehammer, he was of bad health and wanted to stay there because of my father Arnt Steen Brodtkorb, for whom he had been a protege. Arnt Brodtkorb's father, Gerhard Hoe Brodtkorb died young in the ag
2 CONC e of thirty and he spent a lot of his youth in Vardø despite living in Lillehammer with his mother Østine.
2 CONT
2 CONT I met my fathers uncle, Hemming, in 1946 being thirteen years of age, It was school holidays, and I met him outside Hotel Victoria because he wanted to go for stroll to the South Park and back to the hotel where he lived while bui
2 CONC lding his house in Jernbanegaten, By the way, in the hotel he rented the to biggest rooms, one for his wife Solveig and one for himself. He had also ordered a big piano up in his room and the only pianist in the town Halvorsen who
2 CONC  had to be there every day at 12.00 sharp to play for one hour.
2 CONT
2 CONT Having taken the stroll with him, we departed outside Hotel Victoria, standing there he took out his wallet and gave me one hundred kroner saying "get yourself some ice cream!".
2 CONT
2 CONT For two months I took the stroll with him twice a week and every time he gave me 100 kroner. I felt like a millionaire!
2 CONT
2 CONT After three months in Lillehammer Hemming Brodtkorb died and my time as a "millionaire" was for ever over. The town of Lillehammer also lost a big taxpayer!
2 CONT
2 CONT In the bank, Kreditkassen, where my father was the bank manager, his widow and my father found in the safe, a trunk that contained one million rubles. All lost  because and the pomortrade and the russian revolution in 1917. In the
2 CONC  lid of the trunk it was written with nice letters; "Shall be used to decorate the walls in my new study!" I can see him sitting there inn between one million rubles, in 1946 worth nothing!
2 CONT
2 CONT He was in fact a very special man!
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerhard Brodtkorb 21.9.2011.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hemming Brodtkorb bodde i Fæstningsgade 15. Folketelling 1910 foreller at der bodde også Arnt Nicolai (sønn) født 27.2.1896. Dagmar (datter)     født  9.8.1897. Erling (sønn) født 20.7.1899. Helga Corneliussen (Husbestyrer) Agnes 
2 CONC Degerstrøm (kjøkkenpige) Hilde Surjænen (Stuepige) Oluf Bakken (Gaardsdreng).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Wife===
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Brodtkorb/6000000013907505351 Anna Ivertha Zachariassen]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Arnt-Nikolai-Brodtkorb/6000000008018619387 Arnt Nikolai Brodtkorb] - 1896 - Vardø
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Dagmar-Cappelen/6000000013907516659 Dagmar Brodtkorb] - 1897 Vardø - 1932 Oslo
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Erling-Brodtkorb/6000000008018520765 Erling Brodtkorb] - 1899 Vardø
2 CONT
