1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herman_Paus
2 CONT
2 CONT Herman Christopher Paus (4 May 1897 – 11 March 1983) was a Norwegian competitive skier, who was among the pioneers of Nordic combined and ski jumping in the 1910s and 1920s. He later moved to Sweden where he bought the major estat
2 CONC e Herresta near Stockholm from a relative. A relative of playwright Henrik Ibsen, Herman Paus was married to Leo Tolstoy's granddaughter Tatiana Tolstoy-Paus; as such he was the son-in-law of Count Lev Lvovich Tolstoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
