1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Wikipedia==
2 CONT *[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henrik_Ibsen Henrik Ibsen] in Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Henrik Johan Ibsen (ˈhɛnɾɪk ˈɪpsən; 20 March 1828 – 23 May 1906) was a major 19th-century Norwegian playwright, theatre director, and poet. Ibsen was born into the merchant elite of the port town of Skien and had strong family tie
2 CONC s to the [https://www.geni.com/projects/Paus-family/44114 Paus family], an ancient family of clergy and lawyers in Telemark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Already in his lifetime, there was significant interest in Ibsen's biography and family history. Many Ibsen scholars have compared characters and themes in his plays to his family and upbringing. Ibsen himself confirmed that he bo
2 CONC th modelled and named characters in his plays after his own family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both of Ibsen's parents' belonged to the city's and county's elite. Ibsen's ancestors were primarily merchants and shipowners in cities such as Skien and Bergen, or members of the "aristocracy of officials" of Upper Telemark, the 
2 CONC region's civil servant elite. Henrik Ibsen later wrote that "my parents were members on both sides of the most respected families in Skien", and that he was closely related to "just about all the patrician families who then domina
2 CONC ted the place and its surroundings."
