2 CONT
2 CONT '''Christopher Tostrup Paus''', Count of Paus (10 September 1862 – 10 September 1943), usually known as Christopher Paus and also known as Christopher de Paus, was a Norwegian land owner, heir to the timber giant Tostrup & Mathies
2 CONC en, papal chamberlain and count, known as philanthropist, art collector and socialite in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. He gave large donations to museums in Scandinavia and to the Catholic Church. In the Acta Apostolicae
2 CONC  Sedis and the Annuario Pontificio, his name is spelled (conte) Cristoforo de Paus.
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christopher_de_Paus
