1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record and obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=dedekam&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=97173707&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jul. 31, 1917 Oslo Oslo kommune Oslo fylke, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Nov. 3, 2002 Alberta, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Southland Funeral Chapel obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT HANS DEDEKAM 1917 - 2002
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Dedekam, beloved husband of Phyllis Dedekam of Lethbridge, peacefully passed away in Lethbridge on Sunday, November 3, 2002 at the age of 85 years.  Hans was born in Oslo, Norway on July 31, 1917, a son of André and Louise De
2 CONC dekam. He attended school in Oslo and received his High School Diploma.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following graduation he enrolled in University in Paris, France. His studies were interrupted by WWII and Hans was called to serve his country as a soldier of the Norwegian Free Forces between 1942 and 1945. He retired from the Fo
2 CONC rces as a Captain. Upon discharge, Hans returned to University and earned his Degree in Business Administration.
2 CONT
2 CONT He met and later married Phyllis Jespersen in Washington, D.C. on October 20, 1952.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans began his thirty six year career as an administrator with Scandinavian Airlines and worked in Copenhagen, New York and Montreal before retiring in 1982.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans will be remembered as a man of “strong character and gentle nature” and is deeply loved by his family in Canada and Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was predeceased by his parents André and Louise Dedekam and a brother, Anders Dedekam. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Taber Memorial Garden Cemetery  Taber Lethbridge Census Division Alberta, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Bear Hugs Record added: Sep 16, 2012  Find A Grave Memorial# 97173707
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Dedekam, beloved husband of Phyllis Dedekam of Lethbridge, peacefully passed away in Lethbridge on Sunday, November 3, 2002 at the age of 85 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans was born in Oslo, Norway on July 31, 1917, a son of André and Louise Dedekam. He attended school in Oslo and received his High School Diploma. Following graduation he enrolled in University in Paris, France. His studies were 
2 CONC interrupted by WWII and Hans was called to serve his country as a soldier of the Norwegian Free Forces between 1942 and 1945. He retired from the Forces as a Captain. Upon discharge, Hans returned to University and earned his Degr
2 CONC ee in Business Administration. He met and later married Phyllis Jespersen in Washington, D.C. on October 20, 1952. Hans began his thirty six year career as an administrator with Scandinavian Airlines and worked in Copenhagen, New 
2 CONC York and Montreal before retiring in 1982. Hans will be remembered as a man of “strong character and gentle nature” and is deeply loved by his family in Canada and Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides his wife of fifty years, Phyllis, Hans will be forever cherished by his son Hans Eric (Josée) Dedekam and their children, Charles and Elise; a sister-in-law, Marit Dedekam and her four children, Mette, Wenche, Anna-Louise 
2 CONC and Anders all of Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was predeceased by his parents André and Louise Dedekam and a brother, Anders Dedekam.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Funeral Service was held at Southminster United Church, 1011 - 4 Avenue South, Lethbridge on Thursday, November 7, 2002 at 2:00 P.M. with Reverend Frank Lewis officiating. A private family interment took place at the Taber Mem
2 CONC orial Garden on Friday, November 8, 2002.
2 CONT
2 CONT If friends so desire, memorial tributes in Hans’ name can be made directly to the Alzheimer’s Association of Lethbridge, 426 - 5 Street South Lethbridge, Alberta T1J 2B7.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.southlandfuneral.com/obituaries.html?view=obits&id=1471
