1 TITL Flt Lt
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} As of 1936 he was a businessman in Bradford, presumably in his family's export business.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an officer of the Royal Air Force during WWII.
2 CONT *He received his commission as a pilot officer on 27 July 1940: https://www.thegazette.co.uk/London/issue/34949/page/5588/data.pdf
2 CONT *On 27 July 1941 he was promoted to flying officer: https://www.thegazette.co.uk/London/issue/35301/page/5798/data.pdf
2 CONT *On 6 November 1943 he was promoted to flight lieutenant (equivalent of army captain): https://www.thegazette.co.uk/London/issue/36245/supplement/4976/data.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT S/591; 24 Sep 42; P/O (Pilot Officer) A.G. Paus; Spitfire AB427; Up: 08:15; Down; 09:58; Objective: Channel Isles, Cherbourg, St, Malo; Results: Photos of Lannion, Lézardrieux River.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://forum.12oclockhigh.net/archive/index.php?t-49367.html
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Audrey Joan Lee, daughter of Edgar Lee, in Bradford in 1941.
