1 NAME Robert Paus /Platt/ OBE
2 GIVN Robert Paus
2 NSFX OBE
2 _MARNM Platt
2 NICK Robin Platt
1 NAME
2 GIVN
2 SURN
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jerusalem
3 CTRY Palestine
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1905
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 JUL 1946
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jerusalem
3 CTRY Palestine
1 OCCU Diplomat, British civil servant
1 TITL Undersecretary
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Paus Platt, OBE, was Undersecretary in the Palestine Government.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Paus Platt, informally known as Robin, attended Queens' College, Cambridge and joined the Colonial Administrative Service. He became a cadet in Kenya in 1927, was appointed Assistant Resident Commissioner in Mombasa in 1928
2 CONC , became district officer in 1929, then went on to become assistant colonial secretary of Kenya and an assistant secretary in the Colonial Office in London in 1938. He later became undersecretary in the mandatory government of the
2 CONC  British Mandate of Palestine, one of its highest-ranking offices, and was killed in the King David Hotel bombing in Jerusalem on 22 July 1946 as the most senior British official to be killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Platt was the son of Robert M. Platt and Ellen Sophie Paus. His maternal grandfather Christopher Paus, who was a first cousin of Henrik Ibsen, was a Norwegian-born businessman who moved to England, and a member of the noted [http:
2 CONC //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paus_family Paus family]. His other three grandparents were English. He was a nephew of the British Consul in Oslo, Christopher Lintrup Paus, CBE.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Paus_Platt
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Lost his life in the explosion at the King David Hotel, Jeruselam.22nd July 1946.
