0 @N6000000004533374598@ NOTE Henrik Ibsen
1 CONT Ibsen, Henrik Johan (1828 - 1906) born in Skien, Norway. He wasbriefly apprenticed to an apothecary and began medical studies. Attwenty-one Ibsen moved to Christiania (now Oslo). While in Christiniahe wrote his first play, Catalin
1 CONC e.
1 CONT In 1851 Ibsen began managing and playwriting for the National Theaterin Bergen (1851 - 1857). There his writings were largely based on folktales and history. He moved back to Christiania in 1857 to become thecreative director of t
1 CONC he city's Norwegian Theater (1857 - 1862).
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Suzannah Thoresen in 1858.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1863 he and his wife went abroad. He spent the next twenty sevenyears in Italy and Germany (1863 - 1891). During this time abroad, heauthored a number of works, including Brand (1866) and Peer Gynt(1867). While in Munich Ibsen 
1 CONC wrote his groundbreaking realisticdrama, A Doll's House (1879). Ibsen eventually abandoned the realisticstyle of A Doll's House and turned to so-called symbolic dramas. Hecompleted Hedda Gabbler in 1890.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ibsen and Suzannah returned to Norway in 1891. There he finishedwriting The Master Builder (1891).
1 CONT
1 CONT Ibsen died in 1906 at the age of seventy-eight.
1 CONT
